{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2032 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0420182b2ed2a857db0ff49b5c1110aa271c48d390b8c4c5ac2d58bc53876411" :edb/db-before-t 2031 :edb/db-after-t 2032 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535344 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:30:19.030Z" 13194139535344 true] [17592186166895 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344905 13194139535344 true] [17592186166895 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344954 13194139535344 true] [17592186166896 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344914 13194139535344 true] [17592186166896 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344934 13194139535344 true] [17592186167213 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535344 true] [17592186167213 1100 "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ \n{{field-2}}." 13194139535344 true] [17592186167213 1100 "$⟨f(x), g(x)⟩ = \\displaystyle \\int_{- π}^{π}f(x)g(x)dx$\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $[MATH: x ∈ [- π, π)]$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n$⟨\\sin (3x), \\sin (3x)⟩ =$\n{{field-1}}\n\nThe functions $f(x) = \\sin (3x)$ and $g(x) = \\sin (3x)$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139535344 false] [17592186167213 1145 "We begin by using the half-angle identity\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)=\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ $\\text{are not orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." 13194139535344 true] [17592186344905 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344906 13194139535344 true] [17592186344905 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344911 13194139535344 true] [17592186344905 1089 "q-340368" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344905 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535344 true] [17592186344905 1100 "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ \n{{field-2}}." 13194139535344 true] [17592186344905 1113 #uuid "1459f84b-ac32-5a32-9ee7-e5678c3f1aac" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344905 1145 "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{18}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-9\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-0)+\\frac{1}{18}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." 13194139535344 true] [17592186344906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344907 13194139535344 true] [17592186344906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344908 13194139535344 true] [17592186344906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344909 13194139535344 true] [17592186344906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344910 13194139535344 true] [17592186344906 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535344 true] [17592186344906 1041 "field-1" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344906 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344909 13194139535344 true] [17592186344906 1110 #uuid "e719573d-a1ae-52d7-8449-6d6cb14f7307" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344907 1034 "\\pi " 13194139535344 true] [17592186344907 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535344 true] [17592186344907 1111 #uuid "90635441-91e9-5231-82e8-1f7783c24364" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344908 1034 "1" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535344 true] [17592186344908 1111 #uuid "7b385cee-f562-51ce-8889-0cac72fa1968" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344909 1034 "0" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535344 true] [17592186344909 1111 #uuid "d707a58f-d523-53a4-bf56-17c7a61b3c4d" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344910 1034 "-1" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535344 true] [17592186344910 1111 #uuid "82c3a7ac-58b4-55ba-a0c9-59222e0a368c" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344912 13194139535344 true] [17592186344911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344913 13194139535344 true] [17592186344911 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535344 true] [17592186344911 1041 "field-2" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344911 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344912 13194139535344 true] [17592186344911 1110 #uuid "075010aa-4b9b-5ca1-934f-b98275e5e7d3" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344912 1034 "are orthogonal" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535344 true] [17592186344912 1111 #uuid "38b55a66-370d-58db-aa01-d558179ae875" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344913 1034 "are not orthogonal" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344913 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535344 true] [17592186344913 1111 #uuid "78a17764-272d-51ea-a2c4-425663346554" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344914 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344915 13194139535344 true] [17592186344914 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344921 13194139535344 true] [17592186344914 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344927 13194139535344 true] [17592186344914 1089 "q-340645" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344914 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535344 true] [17592186344914 1100 "Let $F(x)={x}^{4}-7x$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{3}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344914 1113 #uuid "13f82e1b-2f3e-536a-8bb2-1fc6ddf6b76a" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344914 1145 "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={a}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344915 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344916 13194139535344 true] [17592186344915 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344917 13194139535344 true] [17592186344915 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344918 13194139535344 true] [17592186344915 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344919 13194139535344 true] [17592186344915 1000 #edb/r