ue] [17592186344954 1113 #uuid "0593ec7c-7f2e-54b5-93d7-d18f56e360e4" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344954 1145 "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(14\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(1-1)+\\frac{1}{2}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." 13194139535344 true] [17592186344955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344956 13194139535344 true] [17592186344955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344957 13194139535344 true] [17592186344955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344958 13194139535344 true] [17592186344955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344959 13194139535344 true] [17592186344955 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535344 true] [17592186344955 1041 "field-1" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344955 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344958 13194139535344 true] [17592186344955 1110 #uuid "46fcd125-ed9f-586c-a5c5-1f7d8614f8ae" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344956 1034 "\\pi " 13194139535344 true] [17592186344956 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535344 true] [17592186344956 1111 #uuid "c1f85280-8e69-5725-84b3-4e2ab7513f5c" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344957 1034 "1" 13194139535344 true] [17592186344957 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535344 true] [17592186344957 1111 #uuid "d88a5898-98df-5333-bc4a-be16b